{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Open Food Facts `brands` is free text, so the same brand arrives as 'Coca",
    "Cola', 'coca-cola', 'COCA COLA'. product_catalog.maker has no brands table",
    "behind it, so whatever lands here is what users read as the subtitle.",
    "",
    "Keys are normalizeSearchText(brand) -- lowercased, diacritic-free,",
    "whitespace-collapsed -- so a lookup survives any casing or accenting.",
    "Anything not listed falls through to titleCaseRo(), which is right far more",
    "often than not; this table is for the ones it gets wrong.",
    "",
    "`drop` is brand fields that mean 'no brand'. They must become null rather",
    "than a maker called 'Unknown'."
  ],
  "canonical": {
    "coca cola": "Coca-Cola",
    "cocacola": "Coca-Cola",
    "coca-cola": "Coca-Cola",
    "dr oetker": "Dr. Oetker",
